# Line endings, pinned.
#
# This checkout has core.autocrlf=true globally and had no .gitattributes, so the working
# tree ended up a mix: some files LF, some CRLF. That combination has a nasty edge —
# `git checkout -- <path>` on an LF file rewrites it as CRLF, after which git reports the
# restored original as modified forever, even though the blob is byte-identical to HEAD.
# Anyone restoring a file after an experiment can lose it that way.
#
# Normalising in the repo and checking out LF removes the ambiguity. It is also why every
# commit here printed a wall of "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The vault is its own repository and pins its own endings; nothing here applies to it.

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
